WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.480
Wanku! Planning Meeting

00:02.480 --> 00:05.230
Wanku! Planning Meeting

00:05.430 --> 00:09.260
Would you give me a break! 
How long is this meeting anyway?

00:09.260 --> 00:10.800
Yeah, it's like I said.

00:10.800 --> 00:13.320
A "secret underground party"?

00:13.320 --> 00:15.950
What are we even supposed to do?

00:15.950 --> 00:17.700
Is it different from Comiket?

00:17.700 --> 00:19.720
I know all about game conventions.

00:19.720 --> 00:21.610
I bet it's like a live fire demonstration.

00:21.610 --> 00:22.790
Oh, very nice.

00:22.790 --> 00:27.100
Every word I'm hearing screams, 
"I've lived my whole life as a loser."

00:27.100 --> 00:27.750
Pretty much.

00:27.750 --> 00:30.000
<i>Yeah, they're basically the same,</i>

00:30.000 --> 00:33.260
<i>but you guys aren't 
in the audience this time!</i>

00:33.260 --> 00:36.230
<i>You're the organizers, so you make it happen!</i>

00:36.230 --> 00:38.390
Yeah, but make what happen?

00:38.390 --> 00:39.900
<i>I'll tell you one more time.</i>

00:39.900 --> 00:43.040
<i>The goal of this event 
is to spread the message</i>

00:43.040 --> 00:45.390
<i>of our Revolutionary Army all around Japan.</i>

00:45.390 --> 00:48.570
<i>The message that the flame 
of otaku still burns bright!</i>

00:48.570 --> 00:51.870
That's easy for you to say. 
You're all talk anyway.

00:52.120 --> 00:54.640
Yeah, you can say whatever you 
want hiding behind that thing.

00:54.640 --> 00:55.820
I know the type.

00:55.820 --> 00:59.700
Dudes who play the role 
but have zero street cred.

00:59.700 --> 01:01.820
Aww, guys, don't say it like that.

01:01.830 --> 01:04.140
I'm going brain dead from the boredom.

01:04.140 --> 01:05.320
That's the problem.

01:05.320 --> 01:08.960
They got carried away 
and decided to throw a party,

01:08.960 --> 01:12.050
but didn't actually have 
any idea how to do it.

01:12.290 --> 01:18.060
Gobo gobo gobo gobo...

01:13.240 --> 01:18.060
"Otaku who've never once taken 
the lead to get anything done

01:18.060 --> 01:20.940
Gobo gobo gobo gobo...

01:18.060 --> 01:20.940
aren't going to know how to take 
the lead to get something done."

01:21.200 --> 01:26.400
Teacher, I think the first thing they need 
to do is realize their own incompetence!

01:26.400 --> 01:29.780
And on top of all that, 
this leader of ours...

01:35.280 --> 01:38.900
Like an elementary schooler hiding
in the back of the class

01:38.900 --> 01:41.920
so he doesn't get called on.

01:41.920 --> 01:43.380
<i>Hey! Otaku Hero!</i>

01:43.380 --> 01:45.670
<i>I know you're there. 
Tell us what you think!</i>

01:45.670 --> 01:48.450
Otaku Hero, what's your take on it?

01:48.450 --> 01:52.580
He's right. You should tell us your vision 
as the leader of the Revolutionary Army.

01:52.580 --> 01:54.840
Um, well, I just...

01:57.010 --> 01:58.600
Hm? What's this?

02:01.600 --> 02:02.850
Whoa!

03:38.980 --> 03:41.990
Tell everyone how much
you like the things you like

03:41.990 --> 03:44.610
Why didn't we think of this sooner?

03:42.620 --> 03:44.610
That's it! Yeah!

03:44.610 --> 03:50.000
This explains what our secret 
underground party is all about!

03:50.000 --> 03:51.660
We knew you'd come through, Otaku Hero!

03:51.660 --> 03:53.020
Our leader!

03:53.020 --> 03:57.500
Take control of our secret 
underground party, Otaku Hero!

03:57.500 --> 04:00.280
Uh, yeah, I'm not so sure.

04:00.280 --> 04:02.480
We're totally depending on you!

04:02.480 --> 04:04.480
You're lead producer.

04:04.480 --> 04:08.040
If we're gonna make Wanku 
happen, we need your help!

04:08.040 --> 04:09.490
We're begging you, Producer!

04:09.490 --> 04:10.530
Producer!

04:10.880 --> 04:14.400
M-Me? A producer...?

04:14.400 --> 04:16.400
Tell everyone how much
you like the things you like

04:18.400 --> 04:19.990
Okay, cool.

04:19.990 --> 04:24.080
For starters, spit out all 
the ideas you brainstormed for Wanku.

04:24.270 --> 04:27.920
There's no reason to be shy. 
Nah, it isn't difficult.

04:27.920 --> 04:32.580
I mean, the important thing is to open your 
minds and let the ideas flow. Am I right?

04:32.580 --> 04:34.170
Wow!

04:32.580 --> 04:34.170
I think he's right!

04:34.170 --> 04:35.910
He really is a producer!

04:37.280 --> 04:40.180
Let's show how much we like 
the things we like!

04:42.280 --> 04:43.000
Wha?

04:44.200 --> 04:46.000
What's gotten into him?

04:46.000 --> 04:47.710
Gobo gobo, gobo.

04:47.710 --> 04:50.180
It's like he flipped a switch or something.

04:54.200 --> 04:57.700
While we're at it, why don't 
we also sell some merch?

04:57.700 --> 05:00.200
Oh? We don't have the funds or know-how?

05:00.200 --> 05:03.400
If we don't give it a shot, 
it's over before it started.

05:03.690 --> 05:06.350
Can't find an underground event venue?

05:06.930 --> 05:09.690
So what? Do we really 
have to do it underground?

05:09.690 --> 05:14.700
Let's build an outdoor stage 
at the Akihabara park ruins and do it big!

05:15.160 --> 05:18.200
Let's show how much we like 
the things we like!

05:18.830 --> 05:35.980
<b>"Can you explain why you agreed 
to produce this 'Wanku' event?"</b>

05:23.300 --> 05:25.370
<i>There wasn't any one reason for it.</i>

05:25.370 --> 05:28.000
<i>Everyone's passion and enthusiasm. 
Everyone's devotion...</i>

05:28.000 --> 05:33.810
<i>When they showed me how they felt, 
no matter how much I searched for one,</i>

05:33.810 --> 05:35.980
<i>I couldn't think of any 
reason to turn it down.</i>

05:39.240 --> 05:41.230
How's the stream prep going, Nick?

05:41.230 --> 05:43.540
<i>It's all coming together. No prob.</i>

05:43.540 --> 05:46.960
How about this, Nick? 
Instead of just streaming it,

05:46.960 --> 05:48.930
why don't we hijack the TV signals and

05:48.930 --> 05:51.240
broadcast our party 
into everyone's living room?

05:51.240 --> 05:55.900
<i>You mean forcing our otaku event 
on demographics that aren't even online?</i>

05:55.900 --> 05:57.750
<i>That's pretty punk, man.</i>

05:57.750 --> 05:59.100
Can you handle it, Nick?

05:59.100 --> 06:01.260
<i>Leave it to this guy, Otaku Hero!</i>

06:02.250 --> 06:04.110
Lead Producer!

06:04.000 --> 06:07.760
<b>Wanku!</b>

06:04.110 --> 06:07.440
Here are the guests who agreed 
to perform at Wanku.

06:07.440 --> 06:10.620
First, the famous anisong 
singer Guts Takako-san!

06:10.620 --> 06:12.890
I'm Guts. It's very nice to meet you.

06:12.890 --> 06:14.900
I enjoyed your work in <i>Frozing</i>.

06:14.900 --> 06:16.560
Great to be working with you.

06:16.560 --> 06:17.770
And over here,

06:17.770 --> 06:20.010
the actress who played Obayashi Zeneko,

06:20.010 --> 06:23.470
the construction site idol heroine of <i>Super 
Galactic Construction Equipment Yunboger G</i>.

06:23.470 --> 06:25.190
It's Homura Yuriri-san!

06:25.190 --> 06:27.020
Great to finally meet you, Yuririn.

06:27.020 --> 06:32.060
We all felt so awful when 
they started oppressing otaku.

06:32.060 --> 06:32.790
But still...

06:33.060 --> 06:35.850
The otaku spirit piles up like falling snow.

06:35.850 --> 06:39.540
Right! And its layers embrace 
the changing times!

06:39.540 --> 06:43.250
We're still getting buried 
in requests to appear

06:43.250 --> 06:46.940
from tons of famous voice actors 
and anisong singers who've been in hiding!

06:46.940 --> 06:49.720
Why don't we take the 
opportunity to film footage

06:49.720 --> 06:52.240
for a physical release like 
a DVD or something?

06:52.240 --> 06:53.670
Great idea!

06:53.670 --> 06:55.480
What do they call it, "mixed media"?

06:55.480 --> 06:58.860
We could do a comic adaptation, 
a film version, an anime,

06:58.860 --> 07:00.710
and get the whole world 
caught up in this thing.

07:00.710 --> 07:01.690
Whoa!

07:02.990 --> 07:06.190
Let's show how much we like 
the things we like!

07:06.980 --> 07:09.490
<i><b>"Performing on an outdoor stage, 
streaming worldwide..."</b></i>

07:09.490 --> 07:11.990
<i><b>"Is it still possible to call this 
a secret underground party?"</b></i>

07:12.030 --> 07:14.740
<i><b>"Isn't the scale of the event 
actually much bigger than that?"</b></i>

07:15.240 --> 07:19.780
<i>Sure, there's really nothing secret 
or underground about it anymore.</i>

07:19.780 --> 07:22.040
<i>But who cares about that anyway?</i>

07:22.040 --> 07:25.580
<i>Who could stop us now, 
when we're riding this big wave?</i>

07:28.220 --> 07:31.530
<i>The most difficult part of being a producer?</i>

07:31.530 --> 07:34.720
<i>Honestly, I've never felt 
any of it was difficult.</i>

07:34.720 --> 07:38.500
<i>If you have the passion, enthusiasm, 
and fire, anything is possible.</i>

07:38.500 --> 07:39.860
<i>Nothing is out of reach!</i>

07:39.860 --> 07:42.940
<i>But the second you give up on it, 
that becomes the final episode.</i>

07:45.240 --> 07:48.280
<i>But isn't that right? 
Doesn't everybody think so?</i>

07:48.280 --> 07:51.370
<i>Don't you want to show 
how much you like the things you like?</i>

07:51.370 --> 07:53.670
<i>So do it! Shout it out!</i>

07:53.670 --> 07:56.500
<i>Shout about how much you like 
the things you like!</i>

08:09.130 --> 08:11.130
<b>O
T
OTAKU
K
U</b>

08:11.130 --> 08:13.130
<b>CURRY RICE</b>

08:11.130 --> 08:13.130
<b>BEER</b>

08:19.150 --> 08:20.720
Whoa!

08:21.210 --> 08:22.900
The day is finally here!

08:22.900 --> 08:25.530
Yeah! It's gonna be 
a huge success, no question!

08:25.530 --> 08:27.520
And it's all thanks to Otaku Hero!

08:27.760 --> 08:29.520
Lead Producer!

08:29.520 --> 08:31.420
Lead Producer!

08:31.420 --> 08:33.110
Lead Producer!

08:37.240 --> 08:38.520
How's attendance looking?

08:38.520 --> 08:41.160
What did you expect? 
We're way over capacity!

08:44.450 --> 08:47.790
Well, then, will you give the introduction?

08:53.590 --> 08:54.440
Yeah, I guess so.

09:10.820 --> 09:12.900
Tell everyone how much
you like the things you like

09:30.630 --> 09:34.550
<b>"Are you at all nervous 
about hosting this event?"</b>

09:34.350 --> 09:35.720
<i>Nervous?</i>

09:35.720 --> 09:38.700
<i>I'm going to have the time of my life.</i>

09:38.700 --> 09:41.080
<i>What do I have to be nervous about?</i>

09:41.080 --> 09:43.040
<i>I think it's going to go great.</i>

09:43.040 --> 09:45.390
<i>My heart's already racing with excitement!</i>

09:45.390 --> 09:46.200
<i>Hey.</i>

09:46.200 --> 09:48.960
<i>So yeah, what I mean 
about saying how much you like—</i>

09:48.960 --> 09:50.690
<i>Hey, Otaku Hero!</i>

09:51.520 --> 09:52.220
Hm?

09:53.530 --> 09:54.240
Huh?

10:05.530 --> 10:07.600
Who the hell are you talking to?

10:07.960 --> 10:09.460
<b>WANKU!</b>

10:11.460 --> 10:12.460
<b>CURRY RICE</b>

10:11.460 --> 10:12.460
<b>BEER</b>

10:15.080 --> 10:17.080
What... is this?

10:25.460 --> 10:26.820
Hey! Otaku Hero!

10:26.820 --> 10:29.170
I know you're there. 
Tell us what you think!

10:29.730 --> 10:32.480
Otaku Hero, what's your take on it?

10:32.480 --> 10:34.980
Um, well...

10:35.440 --> 10:38.990
That's right. That's how it was.

10:39.840 --> 10:42.820
When we decided to host 
Wanku!, our party event,

10:43.560 --> 10:46.330
at first I thought I could 
power my way through it.

10:46.780 --> 10:48.680
But when it came down to it,

10:49.490 --> 10:52.650
when I stopped to think 
about what was going on,

10:52.000 --> 10:55.710
like

10:53.220 --> 10:55.710
I started to get this bad feeling.

10:56.310 --> 10:59.140
I want to celebrate our 
battle victories so far.

10:59.140 --> 11:02.480
To enjoy them with everyone. 
To tell the whole world.

11:02.960 --> 11:04.440
That's what our party was for.

11:04.780 --> 11:06.360
And all these preparations.

11:06.840 --> 11:09.280
But... But...

11:09.600 --> 11:12.100
Is it really the time for that?

11:12.340 --> 11:14.060
To be letting loose?

11:14.060 --> 11:16.580
Gobo gobo gobo gobo.

11:15.280 --> 11:17.620
"Aren't you forgetting something important?"

11:19.240 --> 11:22.280
It's not like we've already won the war.

11:22.280 --> 11:26.530
The fight is only gonna 
get harder from here on out.

11:28.040 --> 11:35.260
Gobo gobo, gobo gobo gobo...

11:28.880 --> 11:31.140
"By throwing a big, flashy party like this,

11:31.140 --> 11:35.250
you're surely going to get more heat 
from the public than ever before."

11:35.250 --> 11:39.210
Shobon is definitely going to 
find out about it, too.

11:39.210 --> 11:40.130
Oh, yeah.

11:40.130 --> 11:43.390
It'll give them a prime 
opportunity to attack.

11:44.640 --> 11:49.650
Basically, I think we're all trying 
to ignore how bad the situation is,

11:49.650 --> 11:52.390
while deep inside we're 
terrified and full of doubt.

11:52.390 --> 11:55.840
Planning a big party, 
as if that's something you'd ever do.

11:55.840 --> 11:58.150
Aren't you just being stupid?

11:58.560 --> 12:01.410
Gobo gobo, gobo gobo, gobogo.

11:59.080 --> 12:02.630
"In other words, all you're doing 
is avoiding reality."

12:11.990 --> 12:15.240
Some part of me realized that. 
I was aware of it.

12:15.790 --> 12:20.220
But the pain of reality, 
the uncertainty of what was ahead...

12:20.950 --> 12:23.040
I couldn't stand to deal with it.

12:23.540 --> 12:25.320
I got too scared to face it.

12:26.200 --> 12:30.980
I mean, we otaku are already 
alienated from the world.

12:31.440 --> 12:35.360
But despite that, throwing a party 
or event or whatever...

12:35.680 --> 12:38.730
Maybe it was a mistake to try to have 
a festival in the first place.

12:39.390 --> 12:42.360
Otaku gods, I'm very sorry.

12:42.360 --> 12:43.560
I won't do it again.

12:43.930 --> 12:46.260
I won't try to throw any parties.

12:46.260 --> 12:47.790
I'm truly sorry!

12:50.000 --> 12:51.990
You shouldn't have to apologize.

12:53.480 --> 12:56.800
Throwing an event like this 
isn't such a bad idea.

12:56.800 --> 12:57.960
Huh?

12:58.660 --> 13:02.840
I think you're right to be worried 
about those things, Otaku Hero.

13:03.240 --> 13:05.560
I've been really worried, too.

13:06.920 --> 13:11.030
Our battles with the enemy have 
actually been getting worse.

13:11.030 --> 13:15.690
Gobo. Gobo gobo gobobobo.

13:12.410 --> 13:15.690
"There is absolutely no reason 
to be holding a festival right now."

13:15.690 --> 13:20.900
But I do understand why you'd want to 
try something like that once in a while.

13:21.840 --> 13:25.200
If you go wild when it's peaceful 
and nothing is going on,

13:25.200 --> 13:27.860
it wouldn't be nearly as exciting.

13:27.860 --> 13:30.240
Although we're at the absolute bottom,

13:30.240 --> 13:33.200
you're risking it all to run 
head-first toward destruction.

13:33.200 --> 13:35.160
You can only do that when you're young.

13:35.160 --> 13:38.760
Let's set fire to the hearts of all 
the otaku out there and go all out!

13:38.760 --> 13:42.540
Into despair, into depression, 
even into hell!

13:42.540 --> 13:44.980
Gobo! Gobo gobo gobo!

13:44.980 --> 13:47.380
Let's highway to the hell!

13:47.380 --> 13:51.570
Anarchy-chan, Blue-chan, Pink-chan.

13:51.570 --> 13:56.620
Hold on a sec, but won't it 
all end in a flash anyway?

13:56.620 --> 14:00.810
If we run from depression for a minute of 
fun without thinking of the consequences...

14:00.810 --> 14:03.140
Then would you rather do nothing?

14:03.140 --> 14:03.940
Huh?

14:03.940 --> 14:08.770
When everyday is a tough battle, 
and you've lost all the joy in life,

14:08.770 --> 14:11.330
the only victory left is a total victory.

14:11.710 --> 14:13.960
Always judging yourself so 
harshly, pushing yourself,

14:13.960 --> 14:17.860
closing off your mind, your heart.

14:17.860 --> 14:20.000
Closing yourself off completely.

14:20.000 --> 14:24.150
Gobo gobo gobo gobo, gobo gobo...

14:21.350 --> 14:25.220
"That probably only leads 
to one thing. Destruction."

14:25.220 --> 14:28.160
Hold on... Wait a minute.

14:28.160 --> 14:31.760
Which one is it? Which one am I in?

14:49.340 --> 14:52.370
What is happening here?

14:52.370 --> 14:54.950
You need to decide. By yourself.

14:54.950 --> 14:56.200
I can't.

14:56.200 --> 14:58.480
Isn't it what you've always said?

15:00.750 --> 15:02.280
To say you like...

15:02.650 --> 15:04.320
...what you want to like...

15:04.320 --> 15:06.330
Gobo gobo bo?

15:06.690 --> 15:09.180
I do want to say it.

15:10.590 --> 15:11.840
I do.

15:12.630 --> 15:14.310
The things I like are...

15:24.690 --> 15:26.860
Wanku!

15:26.870 --> 15:29.410
Are y'all ready?!

15:29.410 --> 15:31.200
Yeah!

15:31.200 --> 15:35.700
Together, we're gonna blow 
the minds of otaku all around the world!

15:37.710 --> 15:40.990
Welcome to the secret 
underground party Wanku!

15:40.990 --> 15:43.150
Let's get started!

15:43.710 --> 15:47.480
First off, the heroine from <i>Super 
Galactic Construction Equipment Yunboger G</i>.

15:47.480 --> 15:50.550
You adored her in her role 
as construction site idol Obayashi Zeneko!

15:50.550 --> 15:53.960
Let's get Homura Yuriri-chan on the stage!

15:56.920 --> 15:58.800
Yuririn!

16:13.860 --> 16:18.110
The crowd is going wild! 
This is a huge success, man!

16:18.110 --> 16:23.420
Yo, things are crazy here, too! 
Wanku! is all over the Internet!

16:23.420 --> 16:27.590
Here, there, even over there. 
It's everywhere!

16:26.250 --> 16:26.840
Wanku

16:27.590 --> 16:29.120
What about the broadcast hijack?

16:29.120 --> 16:30.450
Yeah, I nailed it!

16:30.450 --> 16:35.180
By now, all the non-otaku 
are probably losing their minds!

16:31.720 --> 16:32.670
Wanku!

16:32.670 --> 16:33.550
Wanku

16:36.390 --> 16:37.690
Hmm.

16:38.390 --> 16:42.910
Next up is the leader of our 
very own Revolutionary Army.

16:42.910 --> 16:46.040
Otaku Hero!

17:20.550 --> 17:23.870
<i>Ah, why is it so?</i>

17:23.870 --> 17:27.400
<i>I'm sure you all know what I mean</i>

17:28.160 --> 17:31.590
<i>Right here we have a</i>

17:31.590 --> 17:34.770
<i>Beautiful world all around us</i>

17:34.770 --> 17:39.640
<i>But we get mislead,</i>

17:35.670 --> 17:36.710
W-We're in trouble!

17:36.710 --> 17:37.590
What's wrong?

17:37.590 --> 17:42.400
There are huge armies approaching 
Akiba from all directions!

17:39.640 --> 17:43.430
<i>Mud thrown at our heads</i>

17:43.430 --> 17:47.550
<i>Still even then, I know we'll find</i>

17:47.550 --> 17:53.200
<i>Something to keep holding on to, whoo</i>

17:53.200 --> 17:57.720
<i>Everything happens for a reason</i>

17:57.720 --> 18:00.660
<i>Hold on to your love</i>

18:00.660 --> 18:04.010
<i>Whatever kind of present, 
it all leads to a future</i>

18:04.010 --> 18:07.070
<i>Yeah. This is reality.</i>

18:04.010 --> 18:08.610
<i>That's for you, whoo</i>

18:07.690 --> 18:10.190
<i>It's painful. It's bloody.</i>

18:08.610 --> 18:12.570
<i>Keep on blowin' like a strong wind</i>

18:10.190 --> 18:12.570
<i>There might be nothing but despair ahead.</i>

18:12.570 --> 18:16.250
<i>Keep on fighting until the end</i>

18:14.080 --> 18:15.070
<i>But still...</i>

18:21.070 --> 18:22.330
Tell everyone how much you like

18:22.320 --> 18:23.890
<i>Hey! Otaku Hero!</i>

18:23.890 --> 18:26.330
<i>I know you're there. 
Tell us what you think!</i>

18:35.590 --> 18:37.590
Tell everyone how much
you like the things you like

18:35.590 --> 18:39.230
<i>Living your own life just the way you want</i>

18:39.230 --> 18:43.840
<i>Is what we all want, baby</i>

18:43.840 --> 18:47.020
<i>Because I am what I am</i>

18:47.020 --> 18:54.840
<i>And you are just as you are</i>

19:14.200 --> 19:15.720
Hm?

19:33.020 --> 19:36.840
Magical Destroyers, suckers!

19:33.020 --> 19:36.840
Gobobo gobo-bo, gobo!

19:36.840 --> 19:38.680
Heading straight for destruction!

19:38.680 --> 19:40.890
If you like it, then say so!

19:40.890 --> 19:41.730
Screw it!

19:41.730 --> 19:42.650
Gobobo!

19:42.650 --> 19:45.220
<i>That ain't enough! You're almost brain dead!</i>

19:45.220 --> 19:47.500
<i>Please, please! Asking nicely, please!</i>

19:47.500 --> 19:50.030
<i>Come on, come on, don't chicken out!</i>

19:50.030 --> 19:52.540
<i>Let us hear it, let us 
hear it, take us away!</i>

19:52.540 --> 19:54.900
<i>Violent girls, right here before you!</i>

19:54.900 --> 19:57.260
<i>Let's go crazy! Let it loose today!</i>

19:57.260 --> 19:59.900
<i>Shake, shake, shake off frustration!</i>

19:59.900 --> 20:01.000
<i>Push, push, push!</i>

20:01.000 --> 20:02.260
Don't just stand there!

20:02.260 --> 20:04.760
<i>One two, one two, punchline!</i>

20:04.760 --> 20:07.160
<i>We are, we are party girls!</i>

20:07.160 --> 20:09.600
<i>No one, no one, anti-side!</i>

20:09.600 --> 20:12.640
<i>Pan two, pan two, no panty flash!</i>

20:12.640 --> 20:15.890
Not nearly enough. This ain't even close!

20:15.890 --> 20:18.530
What are you waiting for, magical mosh pit?!

20:18.530 --> 20:22.150
Show us what you got, assholes!

20:26.810 --> 20:31.900
These bandwagoned baby yes-men 
need their diapers changed.

20:31.900 --> 20:34.030
<i>Loser, loser, loser, loser winners</i>

20:34.030 --> 20:36.520
<i>Love their, love their, 
love their, love their freedom</i>

20:36.520 --> 20:38.940
<i>Easy, easy, easy, easy dreamers</i>

20:38.940 --> 20:41.420
<i>Look they're, look they're, 
look they're big complainers</i>

20:41.420 --> 20:43.830
<i>Loser, loser, loser, loser winners</i>

20:43.830 --> 20:46.300
<i>Love their, love their, 
love their, love their freedom</i>

20:46.300 --> 20:48.590
<i>Heaven! Or! Hell!</i>

20:48.920 --> 20:52.180
<i>Rage!</i>

21:02.680 --> 21:04.200
My God!

21:04.200 --> 21:06.020
Is this for real?

21:06.020 --> 21:07.970
It's a miracle!

21:09.670 --> 21:12.830
Wait, were we supposed to 
have other performers?

21:14.820 --> 21:17.810
This isn't a dream, is it?

21:17.810 --> 21:19.040
No.

21:19.040 --> 21:21.550
Your dreams, Otaku Hero...

21:21.550 --> 21:25.300
...gobo bobobo gobo...

21:22.560 --> 21:25.300
"...and the fiery passions
of everyone here..."

21:25.560 --> 21:28.060
...have changed the world!

21:28.480 --> 21:29.230
Yeah.

21:35.100 --> 21:36.600
Too soon!

21:50.480 --> 21:51.540
Huh?

21:52.240 --> 21:54.160
Hello!

23:25.510 --> 23:27.740
Love. It gets heavy.

23:27.740 --> 23:29.880
Love. It sends you flying.

23:29.880 --> 23:32.220
Love. It tears you apart.

23:32.220 --> 23:34.970
Love. It messes with everything.

23:34.970 --> 23:36.470
Yeah, in love,

23:36.470 --> 23:39.970
telepathic fits, smashed into bits.
